{title: O Come, O Come, Emmanuel}
{artist: Latin antiphons · tr. John Mason Neale}
{key: Em}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
O [Em]come, o come, Em[D]manu[Em]el,
and [Am]ransom [Em]captive [D]Isra[Em]el
that [Em]mourns in lonely [D]exile [G]here
un[Am]til the [Em]Son of [D]God ap[Em]pear.

Chorus
Re[G]joice! Re[D]joice! Em[Em]manu[D]el
shall [Em]come to thee, O [D]Isra[Em]el.

Verse 2
O come, [Em]Thou Wisdom from on high, Who orderest
all things [Am]mightily; To [Em]us [D]the path
of knowledge [Em]show, And teach us in [D]her [G]ways to
go. Rejoice! Rejoice! [Em]Emmanuel shall come to [D]thee, O Israel.

Verse 3
O come, [Em]Thou Rod of Jesse, free Thine
own from [Am]Satan's tyranny; [Em]From [D]depths of
hell Thy [Em]people save, And give them [D]vict'ry [G]ov'r the
grave. Rejoice! Rejoice! [Em]Emmanuel shall come to [D]thee, O Israel.

Verse 4
O come, [Em]Thou Dayspring, come and cheer Our
spirits by [Am]Thine advent [Em]here; [D]Disperse the
gloomy clouds [Em]of night, And death's dark [D]shadows [G]put to
flight. Rejoice! Rejoice! [Em]Emmanuel shall come to [D]thee, O Israel.

Verse 5
O come, [Em]Thou Key of David, come, And open
wide our [Am]heav'nly home; [Em]Make [D]safe the
way that [Em]leads on high, And close [D]the [G]path to
misery. Rejoice! Rejoice! [Em]Emmanuel shall come to [D]thee, O Israel.
